{"key":"enterprise/T1205.002","id":"T1205.002","name":"Socket Filters","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1205","tactics":["command-and-control","persistence","stealth"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may attach filters to a network socket to monitor then activate backdoors used for persistence or command and control. With elevated permissions, adversaries can use features such as the `libpcap` library to open sockets and install filters to allow or disallow certain types of data to come through the socket. The filter may apply to all traffic passing through the specified network interface (or every interface if not specified).…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1205/002","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--005cc321-08ce-4d17-b1ea-cb5275926520","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.619Z","source_object_version":"2.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0079","name":"Driver Load","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0079","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3551476e-14f5-4e48-a518-e82135329e03","page":"telemetry/DC0079/"},{"id":"DC0016","name":"Module Load","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0016","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--c0a4a086-cc20-4e1e-b7cb-29d99dfa3fb1","page":"telemetry/DC0016/"},{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0082","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--181a9f8c-c780-4f1f-91a8-edb770e904ba","page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"id":"DC0085","name":"Network Traffic Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0085","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3772e279-27d6-477a-9fe3-c6beb363594c","page":"telemetry/DC0085/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0060","name":"Service Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0060","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--5297a638-1382-4f0c-8472-0d21830bf705","page":"telemetry/DC0060/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0162","name":"Socket-filter trigger → on-host raw-socket activity → reverse connection (T1205.002)","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0162","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--b4cdf164-9cb7-4cad-bdc3-81b5574f364a","relationship_id":"relationship--829a3356-ec45-4101-8eb0-f0c168ff8f03"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0462","name":"Analytic 0462","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0162#AN0462","guidance":"Adversary installs/uses packet-capture or raw-socket capability (WinPcap/Npcap, wpcap/packet DLLs or raw socket attach) and sets a filter. A crafted inbound packet is observed; within a short window the host process that loaded capture libraries initiates an outbound connection (e.g., reverse shell) to the packet origin.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0162"},{"id":"AN0463","name":"Analytic 0463","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0162#AN0463","guidance":"Process creates a raw/packet socket and attaches a (e)BPF filter (setsockopt SO_ATTACH_FILTER/ATTACH_BPF or bpf(BPF_PROG_LOAD)). Immediately after a matching inbound packet, the same process binds/connects outward to a remote host (reverse shell or beacon).","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0162"},{"id":"AN0464","name":"Analytic 0464","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0162#AN0464","guidance":"Process opens /dev/bpf* (libpcap) or loads NetworkExtension filter, then after a crafted inbound packet the same process initiates an outbound connection to the trigger origin.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0162"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0060","component":"Service Creation","name":"WinEventLog:System","channel":"EventCode=7045","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0462","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0162#AN0462","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0060/"},{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=1","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0462","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0162#AN0462","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0082","component":"Network Connection Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=3, 22","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0462","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0162#AN0462","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"component_id":"DC0079","component":"Driver Load","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=6","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0462","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0162#AN0462","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0079/"},{"component_id":"DC0016","component":"Module Load","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=7","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0462","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0162#AN0462","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0016/"},{"component_id":"DC0085","component":"Network Traffic Content","name":"NSM:Flow","channel":"Single, low-volume inbound packet (REJ/S0/OTH or uncommon dport/protocol) from src_ip followed by outbound SF connection to src_ip.","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0462","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0162#AN0462","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0085/"},{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"auditd:SYSCALL","channel":"socket(AF_PACKET|AF_INET, SOCK_RAW, *), setsockopt(… SO_ATTACH_FILTER|SO_ATTACH_BPF …), bpf(cmd=BPF_PROG_LOAD), open/openat path=\"/dev/bpf*\" (BSD/macOS-like) or setcap cap_net_raw.","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN0463","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0162#AN0463","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0082","component":"Network Connection Creation","name":"linux:osquery","channel":"family=AF_PACKET or protocol raw; process name not in allowlist.","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN0463","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0162#AN0463","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"component_id":"DC0085","component":"Network Traffic Content","name":"NSM:Flow","channel":"Rare inbound packet characteristics (ICMP/UDP/TCP to uncommon port) from src_ip followed ≤TimeWindow by outbound SF from same host to src_ip.","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN0463","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0162#AN0463","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0085/"},{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"OpenBSM:AuditTrail","channel":"open/openat of /dev/bpf*; ioctl BIOCSETF-like operations.","platforms":["macOS"],"analytic_id":"AN0464","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0162#AN0464","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0082","component":"Network Connection Creation","name":"macos:unifiedlog","channel":"First outbound connection from the same PID/user shortly after an inbound trigger.","platforms":["macOS"],"analytic_id":"AN0464","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0162#AN0464","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validat